      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "heading": "Three forms of a quadratic",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Standard",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x)=ax^2+bx+c \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Vertex \\((h,k)\\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x)=a(x-h)^2+k \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Factored",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x)=a(x-r_1)(x-r_2) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A — Factoring",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( x^2-5x+6=0 \\).</p><p>Find two numbers multiplying to \\( 6 \\) and adding to \\( -5 \\): namely \\( -2 \\) and \\( -3 \\).</p>\\[ (x-2)(x-3)=0 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x=2 \\ \\text{or}\\ x=3. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.B — Quadratic formula",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( 2x^2+3x-2=0 \\).</p><p>Here \\( a=2,\\ b=3,\\ c=-2 \\), so \\( \\Delta=9+16=25 \\):</p>\\[ x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{25}}{4}=\\frac{-3\\pm 5}{4}=\\tfrac12 \\ \\text{or}\\ -2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
